 "explanation": {
  "state": "check",
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified VAI 840 days before the shortage posting",
  "sentences": [
   {
    "text": "FDA posted the fludarabine phosphate shortage on 2022-05-06 and as of 2026-10-21 it has been on the list for 54 months.",
    "cites": [
     "D8"
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "An FDA inspection of NerPharMa S.r.l. (FEI 3004762406) ended 2020-01-17 and was classified VAI, with the classification letter dated 2021-05-19 — 840 days before the shortage posting.",
    "cites": [
     "D4",
     "E10"
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "The same plant was inspected again on 2024-09-13 and classified VAI.",
    "cites": [
     "E11"
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "A second label names ACTAVIS TOTOWA as the manufacturing plant, but the evidence provides no inspection record for that site.",
    "cites": [
     "E6"
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Corvale East holds 33 units at 7.8 per day for 4 days on hand, while Corvale General holds 136 units at 8.8 per day for 15 days on hand.",
    "cites": [
     "D1",
     "D2"
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "The rule‑ranked first option is to transfer 12 units from Corvale General to Corvale East; Corvale General can spare 12 while keeping two weeks of supply and Corvale East would reach 6 days on hand.",
    "cites": [
     "D5"
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Because the links between labels and plants are weak or some records fail data checks, verify the current manufacturing sites for each NDC and confirm transfer feasibility with the pharmacy director.",
    "cites": [
     "E6",
     "E12"
    ]
   }
  ],
